---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <BaseHead title={"Legends on Screen | " + SITE_TITLE} description="How urban legends and cryptids get adapted into video games and horror films — and what changes, and what doesn't, when a legend gets a screen." />
        <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is Legends on Screen?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Coverage of legends adapted into games and film\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Why do legends become games?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Interactive fear spreads faster than text\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are the movies historically accurate?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Usually loosely adapted, not literal\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What started this pattern?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Slender Man's 2012 indie horror game\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Will this section keep growing?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, updated as new adaptations release\"}}]}"} />
    </head>
    <body>
        <Header />
        <main class="category-page" style="width: 75%; max-width: none; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px;">
        <header style="margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <h1>Legends on Screen</h1>
        </header>

        <section class="category-article" style="margin-bottom: 40px; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8;">
            <p>A legend that stays as a story stays small. The moment it becomes playable or watchable, it reaches an audience that never would have found the original forum post or campfire tale. This dimension tracks how cryptids, creepypastas, and urban legends get adapted into video games and horror films — which details survive the adaptation, which get invented for the screen, and why the game or movie version is so often what people actually remember. New entries get added as new films and games keep mining the same folklore.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="category-wp-content">
<figure class="wp-block-uagb-image__figure"><img decoding="async" src="/media-images/posts/horror-movies-based-on-real-urban-legends.webp" alt="Illustration for Legends on Screen" class="uag-image-legends-screen" width="1200" height="450" title="Legends on Screen" loading="lazy" role="img"></figure>
</section>



<section class="category-keywords" style="margin: 40px 0; padding: 20px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);">
    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 1.3rem;">Related Keywords</h3>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px;">
        <a href="/blog/slender-man-video-game-viral-origin/" class="keyword-btn active" style="padding: 8px 16px; background-color: var(--accent, #B91C1C); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 2px; font-size: 0.95rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; border: 1px solid #fff; transition: opacity 0.2s;">#slender man video game origin</a>
        <a href="/blog/horror-movies-based-on-real-urban-legends/" class="keyword-btn active" style="padding: 8px 16px; background-color: var(--accent, #B91C1C); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 2px; font-size: 0.95rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; border: 1px solid #fff; transition: opacity 0.2s;">#horror movies based on urban legends</a>
    </div>
</section>







<div class="category-faq-section" style="margin-top: 60px; padding: 40px 30px; background: #1A1816; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(185,28,28,0.4);">
    <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px; color: #E8E2D5; font-size: 2rem; font-family: 'Special Elite', cursive;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-content" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px;">

        <div class="faq-item" style="background: #E8E2D5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #B91C1C); box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); transition: transform 0.2s ease;">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-dark, #7A1212); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 400; font-family: 'Special Elite', cursive;">Q: What is Legends on Screen?</h4>
            <p style="color: #2A2723; margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;"><strong>A:</strong> Coverage of legends adapted into games and film</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="background: #E8E2D5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #B91C1C); box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); transition: transform 0.2s ease;">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-dark, #7A1212); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 400; font-family: 'Special Elite', cursive;">Q: Why do legends become games?</h4>
            <p style="color: #2A2723; margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;"><strong>A:</strong> Interactive fear spreads faster than text</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="background: #E8E2D5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #B91C1C); box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); transition: transform 0.2s ease;">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-dark, #7A1212); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 400; font-family: 'Special Elite', cursive;">Q: Are the movies historically accurate?</h4>
            <p style="color: #2A2723; margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;"><strong>A:</strong> Usually loosely adapted, not literal</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="background: #E8E2D5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #B91C1C); box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); transition: transform 0.2s ease;">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-dark, #7A1212); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 400; font-family: 'Special Elite', cursive;">Q: What started this pattern?</h4>
            <p style="color: #2A2723; margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;"><strong>A:</strong> Slender Man's 2012 indie horror game</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="background: #E8E2D5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #B91C1C); box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); transition: transform 0.2s ease;">
            <h4 style="color: var(--accent-dark, #7A1212); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 400; font-family: 'Special Elite', cursive;">Q: Will this section keep growing?</h4>
            <p style="color: #2A2723; margin: 0; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;"><strong>A:</strong> Yes, updated as new adaptations release</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
    </main>
        <Footer />
